licit detachment and cleanup.\n5: - After a timeout, inspect the process and endpoint before retrying or claiming failure.\n6: \n7: ## Linux browser and WebGPU capture\n8: \n9: - Use the preinstalled `playwright-cli` executable from Actions or SSH.\n10: - Use its headed Chromium, persistent Xvfb display, and SwiftShader configuration.\n11: - Run `playwright-cli open http://localhost:3002` for the Pascal development server.\n12: - Load a saved scene. Wait for actual geometry and the active WebGPU renderer.\n13: - Run `playwright-cli screenshot --filename=screenshots/linux.png` after creating the output directory.\n14: - Inspect the image. Reject loading screens, empty grids, and blank canvases.\n15: - Report SwiftShader as CPU software rendering. Do not claim GPU hardware acceleration.\n16: - Inspect `$HOME/.local/share/omgithub-playwright/linux.json` for launch settings.\n17: - Use `playwright-cli --help` for commands and named sessions. Pass configuration only to `open`.\n18: \n19: ## Mobile browser games\n20: \n21: - Support Android and iOS phones and tablets with responsive layouts and usable touch controls.\n22: - Keep gameplay and controls visible within safe areas and avoid browser gesture conflicts.\n23: - Add tilt controls only when appropriate; offer touch alternatives and request iOS motion permission from a user gesture when needed.\n24: - Follow explicit device and control requirements in the user request."}],"metadata":{"truncated":false}},"time":{"created":1794417802995,"ran":1794417803000,"completed":1794417803010}}],"snapshot":{"start":"fc8f8515557d4a7cf6a59989cc6a6faf8ea45b1d","end":"fc8f8515557d4a7cf6a59989cc6a6faf8ea45b1d","files":[]},"finish":"tool-calls","native":{"responseId":"","serviceTier":"default"},"cost":0,"tokens":{"input":3,"output":18,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":5312,"write":397}}},{"id":"msg_1cba2bf130010YI3ARpXuHYgo4","time":{"created":1794417803031,"streamed":1794417807721,"completed":1794417807729},"type":"assistant","agent":"bui